---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CustomPropertiesGenerator from '../../components/CustomPropertiesGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="CSS Custom Properties (Variables) Generator" description="Build a :root block of CSS custom properties from a simple name/value list.">
  <CustomPropertiesGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why CSS variables beat hardcoded values</h2>
  <p>Hardcoding the same color or spacing value across dozens of rules means updating all of them individually when your design changes. CSS custom properties centralize the value in one place — change it once in <code>:root</code>, and every rule referencing it updates automatically.</p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter name/value pairs for your variables (colors, spacing, fonts).</li>
    <li>Copy the generated <code>:root</code> block.</li>
    <li>Reference variables elsewhere in your CSS with <code>var(--name)</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <pre><code>{`:root {
  --primary-color: #10b981;
  --spacing-unit: 8px;
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>Used elsewhere as <code>color: var(--primary-color);</code> or <code>padding: var(--spacing-unit);</code></p>

  <h2>Common CSS Variable Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Forgetting the double-dash prefix</strong> — custom properties must start with <code>--</code>, unlike standard CSS properties.</li>
    <li><strong>Defining variables inside a component's own selector instead of :root</strong> when the value should actually be global, limiting where it can be referenced.</li>
    <li><strong>Using var() with no fallback</strong> in contexts where the variable might not be defined, which silently produces no value rather than an error.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Custom Properties Generator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Centralizing a design system's colors and spacing scale</li>
    <li>Enabling runtime theme switching (light/dark) by swapping variable values via a class toggle</li>
    <li>Reducing repeated magic numbers scattered throughout a stylesheet</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>CSS Custom Properties FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Can custom properties be changed with JavaScript?</strong> Yes — <code>element.style.setProperty('--name', 'value')</code> lets you update them dynamically, which is how many JS-driven theming systems work.</p>
</ToolLayout>
